{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthdayScope","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DiophantineBirthdayScope","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayFaithful"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.not_exists_birthday_separator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.not_exists_birthday_separator","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthdayScope.lean#L114-L121","doc":"The same statement in the form the conjecture would need to contradict: there is **no**\npredicate on ordinals witnessing a separation between two reals of equal birthday. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.no_birthday_only_separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.no_birthday_only_separation","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthdayScope.lean#L100-L112","doc":"**No birthday-only criterion separates two reals of equal birthday.**\n\n`P` ranges over *every* predicate on ordinals, so this covers any separation criterion\nphrased in terms of the birthday alone — thresholds, limit/successor tests, anything.\n\nCombined with Conway's `birthday(√2) = ω = birthday(π)` (cited in the header, not\nderivable from these axioms), this is why `conj:diophantine-birthday` cannot be a\nstatement about `birthday ∘ ofReal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_ofReal_mem_Iic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_ofReal_mem_Iic","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthdayScope.lean#L88-L92","doc":"Both classes of real are confined to the same interval; the axioms distinguish\nnothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_ofReal_le_omega'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.birthday_ofReal_le_omega'","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/DiophantineBirthdayScope.lean#L81-L86","doc":"**Every real embeds with birthday at most `ω`** — algebraic and transcendental alike.\nDirectly the `birthday_ofReal_le_omega` axiom, named here because it is the constraint the\nconjecture has to live inside. ","signatureChunk":0}]}